CODEGEN.md §3.5: a C++ namespace is one scope for all packages emitted into it, so two packages declaring an enum Tone in namespace `sov::gen` collide, reported at the later package's emit.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// A tone.
enum Tone { soft, loud }

emit cpp { out: "@features/a", namespace: "sov::gen", mode: data }
-- b/b.canon --
package b

/// A tone.
enum Tone { high, low }

emit cpp { out: "@features/b", namespace: "sov::gen", mode: data }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8005]  b/b.canon:6:6
  cpp: Tone is generated for both a.Tone and b.Tone

1 error, 0 warnings in 2 packages (…)
